 To change who has access, use `PUT /:account_slug/boards/:board_id` with the `user_ids` parameter.
+
+## Board Publication
+
+Only account admins (including owners) with access to the board can publish or unpublish it. Non-admin board creators cannot change publication. Publishing does not change board membership or `all_access`.
+
+### `POST /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/publication`
+
+Publishes the board. No request body is required. Returns `200 OK` with the board JSON, including its `public_url`. Publishing an already published board preserves its URL.
+
+### `DELETE /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/publication`
+
+Unpublishes the board and returns `204 No Content`. The board's `public_url` becomes `null`, and its public board, column, and card URLs stop working. Publishing it again generates a new secret URL; the old URL remains revoked.
+
+### Public pages
+
+Anyone with the secret URL can view these read-only HTML pages without signing in:
+
+- `GET /:account_slug/public/boards/:key`
+- `GET /:account_slug/public/boards/:key/columns/:id`
+- `GET /:account_slug/public/boards/:key/cards/:number`
+
+Only published cards are visible; drafts cannot be opened directly. Columns and cards must belong to the published board. Invalid or revoked keys return `404 Not Found`.
+
+Treat public URLs as secrets: anyone you share them with can view the board and share the URL with others.
diff --git a/test/controllers/boards/publications_controller_test.rb b/test/controllers/boards/publications_controller_test.rb
